1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,500
Your future does not have to be figured out today.
You only need a next step.

2
00:00:07,500 --> 00:00:15,000
My Next Step – YESS is a website that helps you find that step,
whether you are returning to school, earning credits, waiting for placement, or planning what comes after high school.

3
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:22,500
Start on the home page and choose the situation
that sounds most like you.

4
00:00:22,500 --> 00:00:34,000
You can get help after enrolling, use your time while waiting,
explore choices when you are not sure, check credits, request records, or plan for work and education.

5
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:43,000
There is no wrong place to begin,
and you can return home at any time.

6
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:50,500
On a wide screen, use the menu across the top.

7
00:00:50,500 --> 00:00:58,500
On a phone, tablet, or most laptops,
select the menu button to see every page.

8
00:00:58,500 --> 00:01:06,000
The highlighted item tells you where you are.
You can also use the links at the bottom of every page.

9
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:14,000
Take My Next Step helps you move toward
the right school or program.

10
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:23,000
It has guidance for students who are already enrolled
and students who are still deciding.

11
00:01:23,000 --> 00:01:31,000
Follow the section that fits you, complete one action,
and come back for the next one.

12
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:41,000
The Credits page helps you understand what you have finished,
what is in progress, and what you may still need for graduation.

13
00:01:41,000 --> 00:01:48,000
The Records page explains how to request and send transcripts.

14
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:56,000
Records matter because every completed credit
should follow you to your next school.

15
00:01:56,000 --> 00:02:06,000
Your YouScience results can help you notice strengths
and careers you may not have considered.

16
00:02:06,000 --> 00:02:14,500
Pay for My Future can help you explore financial aid,
scholarships, apprenticeships, and other support.

17
00:02:14,500 --> 00:02:20,000
Cost is an important question,
but you do not have to answer it alone.

18
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:27,500
Continuing your education and earning a high school diploma
can open more doors.

19
00:02:27,500 --> 00:02:37,000
Many employers, apprenticeships, training programs, and colleges
ask for a diploma or an accepted equivalent.

20
00:02:37,000 --> 00:02:46,500
Finishing also shows that you can keep going through challenges,
learn new skills, and complete a long-term goal.

21
00:02:46,500 --> 00:02:53,000
If a traditional high school is not the right fit,
the Adult Education page can help you compare other paths.

22
00:02:53,000 --> 00:02:59,000
After high school, there is more than one good path.

23
00:02:59,000 --> 00:03:08,000
Technical training is hands-on and focused on skills
for a specific kind of work.

24
00:03:08,000 --> 00:03:17,000
A two-year college can lead to a certificate or associate degree,
or help you prepare to transfer.

25
00:03:17,000 --> 00:03:24,500
A four-year college can lead to a bachelor's degree
and careers that require one.

26
00:03:24,500 --> 00:03:34,000
Compare the time, cost, support, and result of each choice.
The best path is the one that fits your goals and circumstances.

27
00:03:34,000 --> 00:03:44,500
The Resources page connects you with help for school and life outside school,
including housing, food, transportation, jobs, identification, health, clothing, and more.

28
00:03:44,500 --> 00:03:55,000
Use On This Page to jump directly
to the kind of support you need.

29
00:03:55,000 --> 00:04:03,000
If you get stuck, open Get Help.

30
00:04:03,000 --> 00:04:10,000
YESS staff can help you understand credits, records,
school choices, training, and college planning.

31
00:04:10,000 --> 00:04:15,500
Asking for help is a strong next step.
Keep learning, keep asking questions, and keep moving forward.

32
00:04:15,500 --> 00:04:20,000
You do not have to know your whole plan.
You just need to know your next step.
